        "original_id": "0f7014e6-a6b8-568d-8d89-f910c5d29c32",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Catuaba infusions, Brazilian drinks, herbal medicine\n- Places: Brazil, South America\n- Languages: Guarani language, Paraguayan Guarani, Tupi–Guarani family, Tupian languages\n- Plants: Erythroxylum vacciniifolium, trees native to Brazil\n- Concepts: Guarani word meanings, aphrodisiacs\n\nFacts:\n- Guarani is an indigenous language of South America, and its primary variety is Paraguayan Guarani.\n- Guarani belongs to the Tupi–Guarani family within the Tupian languages.\n- The term Catuaba comes from a Guarani word meaning \"what gives strength to the Indian.\"\n- Catuaba is used for infusions made from the bark of a number of trees native to Brazil.\n- Erythroxylum vacciniifolium is also known as Catuaba.\n- Erythroxylum vacciniifolium is used as an aphrodisiac in Brazilian drinks and herbal medicine.",
